We model the morning planning problem of a drone delivery start-up as the Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem. We prove its decision version NP-complete through the chain Hamiltonian Cycle $<=_p$ TSP $<=_p$ CVRP, and show that deciding whether the customers fit into $K$ vehicles is a strongly NP-complete Bin Packing problem. We also prove that the Bosphorus-crossing penalty preserves the triangle inequality. We implement, from scratch, a Clarke–Wright baseline, a memetic Genetic Algorithm with giant-tour chromosomes and an exact Split decoder, and a granular Tabu Search with $O(1)$ delta evaluation and adaptive capacity penalties. We derive the asymptotic cost of one generation and one iteration and confirm it on a log–log plot. Under equal time budgets and ten seeds, both metaheuristics reach the best-known solutions of A-n32-k5, A-n45-k6 and A-n60-k9 in every run. On A-n80-k10 the GA has a mean gap of 0.02% and TS 0.25%. Both reach the exact optimum of all tiny instances. The GA is significantly better on the larger instances (Wilcoxon $p < 0.001$).
